  "findings": {
    "packageChanges": "Only declared override maps changed in all three package manifests; scripts and direct dependency declarations are unchanged. Modern glob9\u201314.0.1 maps to14.0.2; modern minimatch9\u201311.0.0 maps to11.0.1. Callable glob7/minimatch3 consumers are preserved.",
    "lockScope": "Native changes are confined to the modern glob/minimatch dependency family, expected path-scurry3 and lru-cache11 maintenance update, brace-expansion/balanced-match deduplication and the matcher dependency. Web/admin upgrade the TypeScript ESLint matcher.",
    "wasiMetadata": "The web lock adds six inBundle/optional/dev child records under @tailwindcss/oxide-wasm32-wasi4.3.3. The entire parent lock record, including version and integrity, is unchanged; none of these child rows introduces a separate resolved artifact.",
    "actualConsumers": "Reviewed Expo fingerprint uses stable Minimatch constructor/pattern/negate/match APIs; Expo config/config-plugins/Metro tooling use supported sync/async discovery APIs. Actual installed regression cases cover their relevant behavior. Node22 CI meets the updated dependency engine requirements.",
    "legacyAdvisory": "All11 retained minimatch3.1.5 source files match the documented hashes. Their source has neither modern preprocessing phase nor optimizationLevel; the advisory-shaped120-segment pattern produces one pattern set. This supports non-applicability of the specifically described amplification mechanism, not a blanket assertion about all vulnerabilities.",
    "fixtureScope": "The three lint fixes add a cleanup-exception comment, remove an unused test helper and record the consumed unoptimized prop in the Next-image test double. No production component, assertion or timeout was weakened."
  },
